 "used_for_features_note": "f_Hz = colleague calibrate() on TRAIN with time_slice (0,1000) (quantised to the 0.5 MHz FFT grid), then refined by 4 iterations of f += slope/(2 pi), slope = |d|-weighted linear fit of the unwrapped phase of the mean difference trajectory d(t) = <z|bit=1>(t) - <z|bit=0>(t) over samples 100..899, z = mixed + 101-tap FIR. theta_rad = -angle(mean over samples 0..999 of d(t)) at the refined f. Both are fitted on the 16000 calibration shots of calibrate() and validated on 16000 independent TEST shots. The unrefined calibrate() f leaves a linear phase drift of the |0>-|1> axis of up to ~190 deg over 2 us, and the colleague theta (computed from the undemodulated trace mean) does not align the axis; both are kept here for reference only.",
